    "html": "<p style=\"margin:0;line-height:1.6;\">Worth 20% of your final course grade. Maximum score: 20 points.</p><h3>Your task</h3><p style=\"margin:0;line-height:1.6;\">Read the scenarios and notice how you approach decisions about digital systems and unequal outcomes. Then use your choices and course learning to explain your thinking.</p><h3>Part A: 15 scenarios, worth 0 points</h3><p style=\"margin:0;line-height:1.6;\">For each scenario, select one option using the numbered selection control. Choose the response that best matches where you would begin. There is no right or wrong selection. The options record your choices; they do not earn or lose points.</p><h3>Part B: four written responses, worth 5 points each</h3><p style=\"margin:0;line-height:1.6;\">Write 3 to 5 focused sentences for each response. Name the requested scenarios and option numbers. Explain your reasoning and apply the course idea or comparison requested. Your written responses carry all 20 points.</p><h3>Before you begin</h3><p style=\"margin:0;line-height:1.6;\">This is an untimed assessment. You can use Save and Close and return to your draft before submitting. There is no requirement to finish in one sitting.</p><p style=\"margin:0;line-height:1.6;\">Use the course materials already available. Work independently. Do not use generative AI to choose or explain your responses.</p><p style=\"margin:0;line-height:1.6;\">You may submit up to two attempts. Your latest submitted attempt is the one I will grade, so include every selection and written answer in it.</p><h3>Build on earlier feedback</h3><p style=\"margin:0;line-height:1.6;\">Before you start, revisit the feedback on Assessment 1. Choose one suggestion that can help your reasoning or use of evidence here. You do not need a grade or feedback on an assignment that is still being marked.</p><h3>How each written response is graded: 5 points</h3><ul style=\"margin:0;padding-left:28px;\"><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px;line-height:1.6;\">Specific scenarios and accurate references to your choices: 1 point.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px;line-height:1.6;\">Clear reasoning that answers every part of the prompt: 3 points. For Written response 3, this includes accurate use of the course idea.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px;line-height:1.6;\">Focused and understandable communication: 1 point.</li></ul><h3>How to complete and submit in Blackboard</h3><ul style=\"margin:0;padding-left:28px;\"><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px;line-height:1.6;\">Open the assessment and select Start attempt. For each scenario, use the numbered selection control to choose one option. You can change your selection while the attempt is open.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px;line-height:1.6;\">Write your answers in the response editors in this assessment. You do not need to upload a document.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px;line-height:1.6;\">Check each selection and written response before selecting Submit. Wait for the confirmation and keep your submission receipt.</li></ul><h3>Privacy and accessibility</h3><p style=\"margin:0;line-height:1.6;\">You control what personal information you share. Remove identifying details about other people. Use readable headings and descriptive links. Add a text description for meaningful visuals, and captions or a transcript for audio or video. Your grade reflects your learning and reasoning; private disclosure and production effects do not earn extra marks.</p><h3>Deadlines and submission window</h3><p style=\"margin:0 0 16px;line-height:1.6;\">Released: October 1, 2026 at 12:01 a.m. Eastern.</p><p style=\"margin:0 0 16px;line-height:1.6;\"><strong>Due: October 13, 2026 at 11:59 p.m. Eastern.</strong></p><p style=\"margin:0 0 16px;line-height:1.6;\">The 48-hour no-penalty submission window ends October 15, 2026 at 11:59 p.m. Eastern. Routine extension requests must arrive before the posted due date, not during this window.</p><p style=\"margin:0 0 16px;line-height:1.6;\">If Blackboard labels work submitted within the allowed window as late, that label does not mean a penalty applies. Work after the applicable window receives zero unless an extension or exception is approved. Unexpected emergencies and approved accommodations are considered separately.</p><p style=\"margin:0 0 16px;line-height:1.6;\"><a href=\"deadline-policy.html\">Read the full Deadlines and Extensions policy</a>.</p>",
