    "html": "<p style=\"margin:0;line-height:1.6;\">Worth 5% of your final course grade. Maximum score: 5 points.</p><p style=\"margin:0;line-height:1.6;\">BFS218 Final Learning Reflection. Weight: 5 percent.</p><p style=\"margin:0;line-height:1.6;\">Return to the question that opened the course: can a machine be racist? Use course ideas and evidence to explain how your thinking developed across the term.</p><h3>What to submit</h3><ol style=\"margin:0;padding-left:28px;\"><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px;line-height:1.6;\">Choose one dated entry or item from your Personal Cartography.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px;line-height:1.6;\">Explain what you believed or noticed at that point.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px;line-height:1.6;\">Explain what you understand differently now using at least one course concept.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px;line-height:1.6;\">Name one question, tension, or practice you will carry forward.</li></ol><p style=\"margin:0;line-height:1.6;\">Submit a focused reflection of approximately 250 to 350 words, or an equivalent accessible audio response. Personal disclosure is not required.</p><h3>Keep this distinct from your map</h3><p style=\"margin:0;line-height:1.6;\">Answer the opening question using one specific earlier idea and one course concept. Do not repeat the whole map or conduct new research. You can use your own completed map without waiting for its grade or feedback.</p><h3>How your reflection is graded: 5 points</h3><ul style=\"margin:0;padding-left:28px;\"><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px;line-height:1.6;\">A specific dated item from your Personal Cartography and a clear explanation of your earlier thinking: 1 point.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px;line-height:1.6;\">Accurate use of a course concept to explain how your understanding changed: 2 points.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px;line-height:1.6;\">A thoughtful question, tension, or future practice connected to your learning: 1 point.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px;line-height:1.6;\">Clear, focused communication: 1 point.</li></ul><h3>How to submit in Blackboard</h3><ul style=\"margin:0;padding-left:28px;\"><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px;line-height:1.6;\">Open this assignment and select Start attempt. Write or paste your written work into the Submission editor using the headings in these instructions. A Word upload is optional.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px;line-height:1.6;\">If you choose a visual format, insert it with a text description or attach it as an accessible file. If you choose an audio or video format, attach the recording and captions or a transcript. A working Seneca OneDrive or Microsoft Stream link is also acceptable.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px;line-height:1.6;\">Keep all required parts together in this assignment. Before submitting, check that your text, attachments, and links open correctly.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px;line-height:1.6;\">Select Submit, wait for Blackboard’s confirmation, and keep the receipt. If you save a draft instead, return to submit it before the deadline.</li></ul><h3>Your work and permitted tools</h3><p style=\"margin:0;line-height:1.6;\">Use your own observations, choices, explanations, and sources. Do not use generative AI to write or rewrite your submission, invent experiences or evidence, or create narration in your place. You may use spelling, dictation, screen-reader, captioning, and accessibility tools that do not generate the course content. Ask me before using a tool if you are unsure.</p><h3>Deadlines and submission window</h3><p style=\"margin:0 0 16px;line-height:1.6;\">Released: December 7, 2026 at 12:01 a.m. Eastern.</p><p style=\"margin:0 0 16px;line-height:1.6;\"><strong>Due: December 13, 2026 at 11:59 p.m. Eastern.</strong></p><p style=\"margin:0 0 16px;line-height:1.6;\">No automatic 48-hour window applies to this final assessment. Routine extension requests must arrive before the posted due date.</p><p style=\"margin:0 0 16px;line-height:1.6;\">Work submitted after the posted deadline receives zero unless an extension or exception is approved. Unexpected emergencies and approved accommodations are considered separately.</p><p style=\"margin:0 0 16px;line-height:1.6;\"><a href=\"deadline-policy.html\">Read the full Deadlines and Extensions policy</a>.</p>",
